--- CLIPPING CENSUS (MEASURED) ---
container max   : 16383 DN. NOT the usable white level (15360) -- these are
                  two different numbers for two different purposes and both are right:
                  15360 bounds the noise model's calibrated range, 16383 is what
                  "this sample is pinned" means. Do not unify them.
ever clipped    : 0.0007% of pixels (58 of 8241504) clipped in at least one frame
always clipped  : 0.0000% of pixels (0 of 8241504) pinned in EVERY frame
                  No pixel is pinned in every frame, so the maximum-severity case
                  M26 measured on coffee-bubbles does not arise on this stack.
                  NOTE 109MSDCF and 119MSDCF are two of the four stacks with NO
                  saturation, and 109 is also the quietest photometrically (M24).
                  A clean result on them is systematically weaker evidence than it
                  looks.

